{"id": "EUVD-2026-76358", "enisaUuid": "3eac7787-f6fc-31fb-b76e-d169845973a7", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niommu/msm: Unwind probe state on registration failure\n\nmsm_iommu_probe() adds its devm-managed IOMMU object to\nqcom_iommu_devices before adding the IOMMU sysfs device and registering\nit with the IOMMU core.\n\nIf iommu_device_sysfs_add() fails, probe returns with the object still on\nqcom_iommu_devices. The driver core then releases the devm allocation,\nleaving a dangling list entry that later list walks may dereference.\n\nIf iommu_device_register() fails, the same dangling list entry remains\nand the sysfs device is left registered as well.\n\nUnwind the sysfs device and global list entry in reverse setup order on\nthe corresponding failure paths.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:43:17", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:47:30", "baseScore": 8.4, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6a1ae472113762f794682229a0f233f1ee0f69a4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/51e37f9179387b6e3fa64a3d3b4fece1a38b3a02", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f532401be9312ecd166f616bb74a65b0b4c150fa", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7f7074a886c4a93e3d12076ce60a510a1ebe400c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/535a200220ca2c83bc8bf54bd2cbe045d6ee70c4"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89452", "GHSA-g6rr-fv4f-cc2j"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "049a447e-bd6f-31af-8ac0-6c6811696fa4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "42df43b36163ed7d0ab13992e411093252903273 <51e37f9179387b6e3fa64a3d3b4fece1a38b3a02"}, {"id": "1e9587be-d262-3426-99fe-8ee6bbd9b4e9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.11"}, {"id": "37102226-3ed5-39e1-8eab-b7726f4e4bb3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "42df